{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And Timna was a concubine.</b> To make known the greatness of Abraham — how much they yearned to attach themselves to his seed. This Timna was the daughter of chieftains, as it says ״וַאֲחוֹת לוֹטָן תִּמְנָע״, and Lotan was among the chieftains of the inhabitants of Seir, of the Horites who dwelt there formerly. She said: I am not worthy to marry you — would that I become a concubine. And in Divrei HaYamim he counts her among the sons of Eliphaz, teaching that he [Seir] lay with his wife and Timna was born of them, and when she grew up she became his [Eliphaz's] concubine — and this is ״וַאֲחוֹת לוֹטָן תִּמְנָע״; and he did not count her among the sons of Seir because she was his sister from the mother and not from the father."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:17.316819608Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}